with complaints of sadness, tearfulness when
alone, and difficulty initiating and maintaining
sleep for the past two months. She works as a
part-time secretary and seems to have
problems concentrating at work. Four weeks
ago, she was started on St. John’s wort tablets
300 mg, 8-hourly, by a naturopath; however,
she has become even more distracted, tearful
and sleepless. The assessment establishes the
diagnosis of major depression but no suicidal
ideation or attempts. Which one of the following
is the most appropriate management option?','{"A":"Add lithium, 600mg daily, to\naugment the effect of St. John’s\nwort.","B":"Add Omega 3, 5 g daily.","C":"Stop St. John’s wort, wait for one\nweek as the washout period, and\nStart her on venlafaxine 75 mg\ndaily.","D":"Increase the doe of St. John’s wort","E":"600 mg 8-hourly."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[117],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-0d6fb69ba7f0","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a6b621c5ecb492405e51","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry (2).pdf","source_page":117,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"a6b621c5ecb492405e51","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":117,"supporting_pages":[117],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mental Health","stem":"A 45-year-old woman presents to your practice\nwith complaints of sadness, tearfulness when\nalone, and difficulty initiating and maintaining\nsleep for the past two months. She works as a\npart-time secretary and seems to have\nproblems concentrating at work. Four weeks\nago, she was started on St. John’s wort tablets\n300 mg, 8-hourly, by a naturopath; however,\nshe has become even more distracted, tearful\nand sleepless. The assessment establishes the\ndiagnosis of major depression but no suicidal\nideation or attempts. Which one of the following\nis the most appropriate management option?","options":{"A":"Add lithium, 600mg daily, to\naugment the effect of St. John’s\nwort.","B":"Add Omega 3, 5 g daily.",