Started on fluoxetine for treatment of major
depression, diagnosed based on findings of
low mood, decreased sleep and appetite and
loss of concentration. Today, he has
presented because, even though his
depressive symptoms have
Satisfactorily improved with treatment, he
has been experiencing terrifying sleep
disturbances. He explains that he wakes up in
the middle of the night and sees scary black
figures around his bed. He wants to get off
the bed but is unable to do so. He cannot
even move a finger, shout or call for help. The
whole experience is so frightening that he is
afraid of going to sleep at all. He does not
have such a problem while awake. Which one
of the following is the most appropriate
management for him?','{"A":"Reassure that this is normal and\nresolves with time.","B":"Add an antipsychotic medication.","C":"Advise that he uses a sleep mask\nduring sleep.","D":"Switch to another antidepressant.","E":"Advise sleep hygiene and routine."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[179,180],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-c17117e5676a","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"ae5cb8b68d68a284e0f2","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry (2).pdf","source_page":179,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_cross_page_option_stitch","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"ae5cb8b68d68a284e0f2","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Psychiatry (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":179,"supporting_pages":[179,180],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mental Health","stem":"Michael, 35 years old, has recently been\nStarted on fluoxetine for treatment of major\ndepression, diagnosed based on findings of\nlow mood, decreased sleep and appetite and\nloss of concentration. Today, he has\npresented because, even though his\ndepressive symptoms have\nSatisfactorily improved with treatment, he\nhas been experiencing terrifying sleep\ndisturbances. He explains that he wakes up in\nthe middle of the night and sees scary black\nfigures around his bed. He wants to get off\nthe bed but is unable to do so. He cannot\neven move a finger, shout or call for help. The\nwhole experience is so frightening that he is\nafraid of going to sleep at all. He does not\nhave such a problem while awake. Which one\nof the following is the most appropriate\nmanagement for him?