emergency department with a complaint of
chest pain that turned out to be of cardiac
origin. Electrocardiographic changes
were consistent with inferior ST-elevation
myocardial infarction (STEMI). He
underwent coronary artery bypass graft the
next day. He is a commercial driver and, on
discharge, wants to know if he can continue
driving. Which one of the following would be
the most appropriate advice?','{"A":"can drive private and\ncommercial vehicles as long as he\nfeels fine.","B":"should write a letter to road\nSafety department.","C":"commercial driving for\nfour weeks.","D":"commercial driving for\nthree months.","E":"can never drive commercial\nvehicles, but he can drive private\nvehicles after three months."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[126,127],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-a85bb0452a56","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"814cc6fd4f36022d88a6","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (1).pdf","source_page":126,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_cross_page_option_stitch","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"814cc6fd4f36022d88a6","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":126,"supporting_pages":[126,127],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Ethics/Population Health","stem":"A 65-year-old man presented to the\nemergency department with a complaint of\nchest pain that turned out to be of cardiac\norigin. Electrocardiographic changes\nwere consistent with inferior ST-elevation\nmyocardial infarction (STEMI). He\nunderwent coronary artery bypass graft the\nnext day. He is a commercial driver and, on\ndischarge, wants to know if he can continue\ndriving. Which one of the following would be\nthe most appropriate advice?","options":{"A":"can drive private and\ncommercial vehicles as long as he\nfeels fine.","B":"should write a letter to road\nSafety department.","C":"commercial driving for\nfour weeks.","D":"commercial driving for\nt